arryover tests", "score": 0.663, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPS-058 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-APPA-001", "request matches RQC:RQC-002 (0.68); FAM:SF-APPA-001 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-002"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "If the A1 adapter PPP lift is real coverage response, wrong-way teams should do worse than no-signal teams, the gap should widen with scheme-vote confidence, and adapting in Game N should carry over to Game N+1.", "observed_result": "T1 dPPP: adapter +0.0667 (n=205), neutral +0.0248 (n=50), no_signal +0.1260 (n=57), wrong_way +0.0111 (n=274). T2: adapter minus no-signal -0.0361 (1 vote), -0.1170 (2 votes). T3 next-game PPP Welch t=-1.003, p=0.842; MW [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF13", "label": "Study family SF13: Within-game did_adapt toward SHOULD counters improves PPP", "score": 0.505, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-002 (0.68); FAM:SF13 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-002", "request matches VAR:three_point_attempts_or_luck (0.67); FAM:SF13 auto_measures VAR:three_point_attempts_or_luck"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Within-game did_adapt toward SHOULD counters improves PPP", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Offenses that shift toward the counter play types for the inferred opponent scheme gain PPP later in the game.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-003] 531 rows with inferred scheme; 249 adapted (46.9%); adapters +0.0701 (n=239) vs non-adapters +0.0121 (n=269), advantage +0.0580 PPP; DROP +0.1001, SWITCH -0.0436, HELP +0.0450.", "[APPM-013] Adapter dPPP +0.0613 vs +0.0131; advantage +0.0482 PPP, p=0.0199. SWITCH subgroup reversed (-0.0160).", "[CHT-018] First run: adapters n=229 mean dPPP +0.0613 vs non-adapters; later 586 rows, 90.6% inferable, adapters +0.0701 vs non-adapters +0.0121, lift +0.058 (n=508). T1: no-signal baseline is highest dPPP so +0.05 lift  [cut; read_family for the full text]"]}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "score": 0.439, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-055 (0.70); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-055"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.", "observed_result": "Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n>=30 for lineup cells cited", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-012", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-012: Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs", "score": 0.425, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-049 (0.67); FAM:SF-APPS-012 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-049"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Playoff defenses suppress DRIVE more than RS defenses (both lower PPP allowed and lower share).", "observed_result": "DRIVE allowed 1.191 -> 0.923 (-0.268), share 21.2% -> 18.2%; PNR -0.139, share +12.1pp; PULL_UP +0.341, share -7.6pp.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No inferential test; PNR share jump of +12.1pp may reflect tagging differences.", "observed_sample_and_power": "25 teams", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "25 defensive teams, min 30 poss per cell; RS vs playoff PPP allowed and opponent possession share by PT.", "observed_verdict": "descriptive", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}]}], "n_results": 10}

